WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.411
Bring the fictional people map, listening notes, message, readiness support and pilot design together.

00:00:06.411 --> 00:00:13.738
The prototype is accurate, but the message promises an immediate start while participant access remains unresolved.

00:00:13.738 --> 00:00:18.317
A practical resource describes a tool the worker cannot reach.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:21.065
That mismatch is evidence for revision.

00:00:21.065 --> 00:00:23.812
Retain each source and approval status.

00:00:23.812 --> 00:00:29.766
AI-generated listening reactions remain simulated, and the pilot still needs actual human permission.

00:00:29.766 --> 00:00:40.298
The fictional manager owns the pilot decision, the coordinator monitors questions, the reviewer checks and stops, and the policy owner handles access concerns.

00:00:40.298 --> 00:00:45.335
For your continuing project, compare the artifacts without replacing earlier work.

00:00:45.335 --> 00:00:52.204
Find the condition that prevents the plan from working for the person with least authority.

00:00:52.204 --> 00:01:00.447
A complete set of documents is useful, but it does not by itself prove readiness or staff acceptance.
